msgctxt "LOGIN) can be resent as another user of the hub."
msgid ""
"Saves central refused, added up across the hubs still in use, by kind, "
"programme and error code. Once the cause is fixed on central (a setting, an "
"option, someone's access), Resend asks every hub to send that group's "
"refused saves again, as their original authors, at its next sync. Central's "
"new answer stands; a save it refuses again shows up here as a fresh "
"refusal. Saves whose author could not log in online for 7 days after "
"central stopped accepting their token (error code NO"
msgstr ""
"Saves central refused, added up across the hubs still in use, by kind, "
"programme and error code. Once the cause is fixed on central (a setting, an "
"option, someone's access), Resend asks every hub to send that group's "
"refused saves again, as their original authors, at its next sync. Central's "
"new answer stands; a save it refuses again shows up here as a fresh "
"refusal. Saves whose author could not log in online for 7 days after "
"central stopped accepting their token (error code NO_LOGIN) can be resent "
"as another user of the hub."

msgctxt ""
"facilityhub, and read access to the hub accounts group. Each hub makes its "
"registry entry writable by the hub owners group (staff who set hubs up, "
"take them over or replace them), the hub accounts group and the hub "
"managers only, once the hub owners group is named. Only superusers change "
"these settings, and the hub managers and hub owners groups only until they "
"are named."
msgid ""
"Each approved hub gets a user in this group (write sharing on the "
"facility-hub namespaces, except facility-hub-admin) with this role, which "
"must have no authorities. Members of the hub managers group approve hubs "
"and make move codes without being superusers; they need a role with "
"F_USER_ADD, F_USER_VIEW, F_USER_GROUPS_READ_ONLY_ADD_MEMBERS and M"
msgstr ""
"Each approved hub gets a user in this group (write sharing on the "
"facility-hub namespaces, except facility-hub-admin) with this role, which "
"must have no authorities. Members of the hub managers group approve hubs "
"and make move codes without being superusers; they need a role with "
"F_USER_ADD, F_USER_VIEW, F_USER_GROUPS_READ_ONLY_ADD_MEMBERS and "
"M_facilityhub, and read access to the hub accounts group. Each hub makes "
"its registry entry writable by the hub owners group (staff who set hubs up, "
"take them over or replace them), the hub accounts group and the hub "
"managers only, once the hub owners group is named. Only superusers change "
"these settings, and the hub managers and hub owners groups only until they "
"are named."

